meta {
  name: Space Notify Write
  type: http
  seq: 162
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/xrpc/com.atproto.space.notifyWrite
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{serviceAuthToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "space": "at://did:plc:authorityaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa/space/org.example.bucket/main",
    "repo": "did:plc:memberaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa",
    "rev": "3kabcdefghij2",
    "hash": { "$bytes": "BwcHBwcHBwcHBwcHBwcHBwcHBwcHBwcHBwcHBwcHBwc=" }
  }
}

docs {
  A repo host telling a space host that one of its repos advanced, so the authority can maintain
  the rev/hash listRepos reports. The space host then forwards the notification to every service
  registered through registerNotify. Carries no record data — just the new rev and commit hash.

  Authenticated with service auth (Authorization: Bearer <service-auth JWT>, lxm =
  com.atproto.space.notifyWrite, aud = this server's DID). Unlike uploadBlob's service-auth
  path, the issuer is deliberately NOT required to be a local account — a repo host is somewhere
  else by definition. It must be either the repo whose head moved or the space's authority
  forwarding; anyone else is 401.

  Best-effort by lexicon (it declares no errors): a notification about a space this server is not
  the authority for is accepted and dropped.
}
